# Serve the landing page at the site root.
#
# Cloudflare's asset config here uses html_handling = "none", so paths are
# served exactly as written -- /app.html comes from /app.html with no redirect
# hop. That is deliberate: sw.js precaches explicit ".html" paths, and
# precaching a URL that 307s to somewhere else is fragile.
#
# The cost of literal paths is that "/" no longer maps to index.html on its
# own, which returned a bare 404 on the workers.dev deploy. This restores it
# as a 200 rewrite rather than a redirect, so the address bar stays on "/"
# and nothing gains an extra round trip.
#
# Same file format on Netlify and Cloudflare, so this is correct on whichever
# host is serving.
/    /index.html    200
